WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.754
Open a new temporary chat and upload the chapter PDF.

00:00:04.754 --> 00:00:06.335
ChatGPT reads the uploaded chapter · accelerated.

00:00:06.335 --> 00:00:09.835
Write the prompt · fast typing.

00:00:09.835 --> 00:00:10.174
Send the shortcut as the second message.

00:00:10.174 --> 00:00:12.960
ChatGPT processes the prompt and builds the widget · accelerated.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.627
Inspect the generated widget before using its controls.

00:00:16.635 --> 00:00:25.385
Write a concise distinction that could be expanded in an oral answer.

00:00:25.385 --> 00:00:28.663
Reveal the expected answer and compare the key concepts.

00:00:28.663 --> 00:00:31.963
Advance to the second oral-exam question.

00:00:31.963 --> 00:00:40.112
Explain why using a new definition does not establish weight updates.

00:00:40.112 --> 00:00:45.556
Compare the explanation with the chapter-grounded expected answer.

00:00:45.556 --> 00:00:48.847
Advance to the third oral-exam question.

00:00:48.847 --> 00:00:56.867
Summarize how prediction error guides parameter updates in pretraining.

00:00:56.867 --> 00:01:02.326
Reveal the expected account of the training mechanism.

00:01:02.326 --> 00:01:06.740
Go Back to verify that the earlier written answer is retained.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:11.196
Return to the third question and its stored explanation.

00:01:11.196 --> 00:01:13.783
Continue to the fourth question.

00:01:13.783 --> 00:01:22.157
Explain the purpose of keeping the model fixed while varying the input.

00:01:22.157 --> 00:01:27.586
Reveal the expected reasoning for the controlled comparison.

00:01:27.586 --> 00:01:30.839
Advance to the fifth question.

00:01:30.839 --> 00:01:40.130
Distinguish retrieval from parameter updates and ordinary model calculations.

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:43.356
Reveal and compare the final expected answer.

00:01:43.356 --> 00:01:50.556
Restart the oral-practice set for another attempt.
